  "title": "NASA's Boeing Crew Flight Test Astronauts Talk with NASA Leadership – Monday, June 10, 2024",
  "description": "NASA astronauts Butch Wilmore and Suni Williams discussed living and working in space as part of the Crewed Flight Test (CFT) of the Boeing Starliner spacecraft during an in-flight interview with NASA leaders including Administrator Bill Nelson, deputy Administrator Pam Melroy, and Director of the Johnson Space Center, Vanessa Wyche on June 10. Wilmore and Williams are in the midst of completing a test flight to check out Starliner’s systems ahead of spacecraft certification. The duo will remain at the space station for about a week to complete a series of test objectives before departing the complex for a landing in the Southwestern United States.   Join NASA as we go forward to the Moon and on to Mars -- discover the latest on Earth, the Solar System and beyond with a weekly update in your inbox.  Subscribe at: https://www.nasa.gov/subscribe",
